{
  "info": {
    "name": "ShopForge — Auth & RBAC",
    "_postman_id": "shopforge-auth-rbac-v1",
    "description": "KAN-12: JWT auth + RBAC for Customer, Vendor, and SuperAdmin roles.\n\n## Seed credentials (Password@123 for all)\n- SuperAdmin: superadmin@shopforge.io\n- Vendor (TechGadgets Pro): vendor@techgadgetspro.com  |  tenant_id: a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000001\n- Vendor (Urban Threads): vendor@urbanthreads.io  |  tenant_id: a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000002\n- Customer (TechGadgets Pro): alice.chen@example.com  |  tenant_id: a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000001\n- Customer (Urban Threads): chloe.d@example.com  |  tenant_id: a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000002\n\n## Workflow\n1. Run a login request — the test script saves the token to {{token}} automatically.\n2. All protected requests read {{token}}.\n3. Customer login requires {{tenant_id}} — same email can exist on different storefronts.\n4. Set {{baseUrl}} to your server, e.g. http://localhost:4000",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    {
      "key": "tenant_id",
      "value": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000001",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Active tenant ID (TechGadgets Pro). Change to test Urban Threads."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🌐 Public — Registration & Login",
      "description": "No authentication required.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Vendor — Register (creates storefront + user)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('success flag true', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().success).to.be.true);",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const t = pm.response.json().data.tenant;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('tenant_id', t.id);",
                  "  console.log('New tenant_id saved:', t.id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"first_name\": \"Alice\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Vendor\",\n  \"email\": \"alice.vendor@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Password@123\",\n  \"store_name\": \"Alice's Gadgets\",\n  \"store_slug\": \"alices-gadgets\",\n  \"contact_email\": \"hello@alicesgadgets.com\",\n  \"contact_phone\": \"+1-415-555-9999\",\n  \"business_address\": \"123 Market St, San Francisco, CA\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "vendor", "register"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Vendor — Login (seed: TechGadgets Pro)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('token present', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().data.token);",
                  "  console.log('Vendor token saved. tenant_id:', pm.response.json().data.user.tenant_id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
